Description: Bayesian inference for separable temporal exponential random
    graph models (STERGMs) of dynamic binary networks and for the separable
    two-layer STERGMs of dynamic signed networks (Caimo and Gollini, 2025,
    <doi:10.48550/arXiv.2505.07669>). Each transition is decomposed into the
    formation and persistence of ties (and, for signed networks, of their
    signs); the resulting doubly-intractable posteriors are sampled with
    approximate exchange algorithms based on adaptive Metropolis-Hastings or
    adaptive direction sampling. Signed-network statistics (geometrically
    weighted edgewise shared friends and enemies, negative degree, signed
    triangles) are implemented natively in C for fast auxiliary network
    simulation. Posterior predictive goodness of fit, diagnostics of the
    auxiliary simulations, simulation and forecasting tools are provided.
